        <main class="main-content">

            <div class="intro-card">
                <div class="intro-card-icon">📋</div>
                <p><strong>Summary:</strong> Scoutix is operated by Muhammad Mohsin Shabbir, a sole proprietor based in Islamabad, Pakistan. We collect your account, billing, and usage data to run our lead generation platform. We aggregate publicly available business information from online sources. We do not sell your personal data. You may contact <strong>support@scoutix.io</strong> at any time to exercise your data rights.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="overview">
                <div class="section-number">Section 01</div>
                <h2>Overview &amp; Data Controller</h2>
                <p>This Privacy Policy describes how Scoutix ("Scoutix," "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information obtained through the Scoutix platform and website (collectively, the "Service").</p>

                <div class="info-box">
                    <strong>Data Controller:</strong> Muhammad Mohsin Shabbir<br>
                    Operating under the trading name: <strong>Scoutix</strong><br>
                    Address: Islamabad, Pakistan<br>
                    Contact: support@scoutix.io<br><br>
                    Scoutix is operated as a sole proprietorship. There is no registered company entity at this time. Muhammad Mohsin Shabbir is personally responsible for data handling practices described in this policy.
                </div>

                <p><strong>Role Clarification:</strong> Muhammad Mohsin Shabbir / Scoutix acts as a <em>data controller</em> for personal data collected directly from users (account, billing, and usage data). For publicly available business contact data that users search and export through the platform, Scoutix functions as a data processing tool only — the user assumes full responsibility for how that exported data is subsequently used.</p>
                <p>By creating an account or using the Service, you agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, please discontinue use of the Service.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="information-we-collect">
                <div class="section-number">Section 02</div>
                <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
                <p>We collect information you provide directly, information generated automatically through your use of the Service, and publicly available business data that our platform aggregates from online sources.</p>
                <div class="data-grid">
                    <div class="data-card">
                        <h4>👤 Account Information</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Full name</li>
                            <li>Email address</li>
                            <li>Password (hashed — never stored in plain text)</li>
                            <li>Account creation date</li>
                            <li>Subscription plan</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="data-card">
                        <h4>💳 Billing Information</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Subscription tier selected</li>
                            <li>Transaction records and receipts</li>
                            <li>Billing country / region</li>
                            <li>Payment method type (card brand only)</li>
                            <li>Card details handled exclusively by Paddle — we do not store card numbers</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="data-card">
                        <h4>📊 Usage &amp; Activity Data</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Search queries and filters used</li>
                            <li>Features and tools accessed</li>
                            <li>Export history and volume</li>
