            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="how-we-use">
                <div class="section-number">Section 03</div>
                <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>

                <h3>Service Delivery</h3>
                <p>We use your account and usage data to authenticate your sessions, process lead generation queries, generate results, and enable data export functionality. This processing is necessary to fulfil our contractual obligations to you as a subscriber.</p>

                <h3>Billing &amp; Subscription Management</h3>
                <p>Billing data is used to process subscription payments, issue invoices, manage plan changes, handle cancellations, and prevent fraudulent transactions. Payment processing is handled entirely by Paddle; we receive only transaction confirmation and subscription status data.</p>

                <h3>Service Improvement</h3>
                <p>Aggregated and anonymized usage data helps us identify performance issues, understand feature adoption, and improve the platform experience. We do not use individual-level data for product analytics without consent.</p>

                <h3>Communication</h3>
                <p>We send transactional emails including account confirmations, subscription receipts, password resets, and service notifications. Where you have opted in, we may also send product updates or promotional communications. You may unsubscribe from marketing emails at any time using the unsubscribe link in those emails.</p>

                <h3>Fraud Prevention &amp; Security</h3>
                <p>IP addresses and usage patterns are monitored to detect and prevent unauthorized access, platform abuse, and fraudulent activity, based on our legitimate interest in maintaining a secure and reliable service.</p>

                <h3>Legal Basis for Processing (GDPR — EEA / UK Users)</h3>
                <p>For users in the European Economic Area (EEA) or United Kingdom, we process personal data on the following legal bases:</p>
                <p><strong>Contractual Necessity (Article 6(1)(b)):</strong> Account registration data, login credentials, and billing information are processed to perform our contract with you and deliver the Service.</p>
                <p><strong>Legitimate Interest (Article 6(1)(f)):</strong> Security monitoring, fraud prevention, and aggregate analytics are processed on the basis of our legitimate interest in operating a safe and functional platform, balanced against your privacy rights.</p>
                <p><strong>Consent (Article 6(1)(a)):</strong> Where you have opted in to receive marketing communications, we process your email on the basis of your freely given consent. You may withdraw consent at any time by using the unsubscribe link in any marketing email.</p>

                <h3>Lawful Basis for Publicly Available Business Data Aggregation</h3>
                <p>The business information surfaced through Scoutix (names, addresses, phone numbers, categories, ratings) is sourced from publicly accessible online directories. This data relates to businesses as commercial entities, not to private individuals in their personal capacity. Our processing of such publicly available business data to provide search and export functionality to subscribers is based on our legitimate interest in delivering the agreed service, and is consistent with the reasonable expectations of both users and the businesses whose public-facing contact details appear in public directories.</p>
                <p>Scoutix does not process special category personal data and does not use publicly available data to build profiles of private individuals.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="data-sources">
                <div class="section-number">Section 04</div>
                <h2>Data Sources — Publicly Available Business Information</h2>
                <p>The core functionality of Scoutix involves aggregating publicly available business information from online directories and mapping services. The types of business data our platform surfaces include:</p>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    🏢 Business names · Physical addresses · Phone numbers · Business websites · Business categories · Operational hours · Public ratings and review counts
                </div>
                <p>This information is publicly accessible on the open internet and relates primarily to businesses and commercial entities. Scoutix does not claim ownership of this third-party data. Users are solely responsible for ensuring their use of exported business data complies with all applicable laws in their jurisdiction and in the jurisdictions they target, including anti-spam regulations, telemarketing laws, and local data protection requirements.</p>
                <p>Scoutix does not guarantee the accuracy, completeness, or current validity of publicly sourced business data, as such information is subject to change by the original source at any time.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="storage-security">
                <div class="section-number">Section 05</div>
                <h2>Data Storage &amp; Security</h2>
                <p>Your account data, billing records, and usage data are stored on secure cloud infrastructure maintained by reputable third-party hosting providers. We implement the following security practices:</p>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    🔐 Encrypted data transmission (HTTPS / TLS) · Password hashing using industry-standard algorithms · Role-based access controls · Secure session management · Regular security reviews and monitoring
                </div>
                <p>While we apply reasonable and appropriate technical measures to protect your data, no system can be guaranteed 100% secure. In the event of a data breach that poses a material risk to your rights, we will notify affected users in a timely manner consistent with applicable law.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="third-party">
                <div class="section-number">Section 06</div>
                <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
                <p>Scoutix uses the following categories of third-party service providers to operate the platform. Each provider processes data under their own privacy policies and applicable data processing agreements.</p>

                <h3>Cloud Hosting Providers</h3>
                <p>We use cloud infrastructure providers to host our application servers, databases, and static assets. These providers may process data in data centers located in various countries.</p>

                <h3>Payment Processing — Paddle</h3>
                <p>Subscription billing is managed by Paddle (paddle.com), a third-party Merchant of Record. Paddle processes payment card data and issues invoices on our behalf. Your financial data is subject to Paddle's Privacy Policy. We do not store or have direct access to your full payment card details. Refunds are handled in accordance with our Terms of Service and Paddle's applicable payment terms.</p>

                <h3>Email Delivery</h3>
                <p>We use a third-party transactional email provider to deliver account notifications, receipts, and communications. Email providers may process your email address and delivery metadata.</p>

                <h3>Analytics</h3>
                <p>We may use analytics tools to understand aggregate platform usage. Where used, these tools are configured to operate on anonymized or pseudonymized data. We do not enable cross-site behavioral tracking or sell user data to advertisers.</p>

                <h3>Infrastructure &amp; Automation Services</h3>
                <p>To deliver our data aggregation functionality, Scoutix uses server-side cloud infrastructure including proxy routing services and automation components. These tools are used to facilitate user-requested data queries across publicly available online sources on behalf of users. No personal data of our users is shared with these infrastructure providers beyond what is technically necessary to route and process requests.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="international-transfers">
                <div class="section-number">Section 07</div>
                <h2>International Data Transfers</h2>
                <p>Scoutix is operated from Islamabad, Pakistan and serves users across multiple countries. Your data may be processed in countries other than your country of residence, including countries where data protection laws may differ from those in your jurisdiction.</p>
                <p>When processing data from users in the European Economic Area (EEA) or United Kingdom, international transfers are carried out where necessary for the performance of our contract with you and subject to appropriate safeguards consistent with applicable data protection laws. By using the Service, you acknowledge that your data may be transferred to and processed in Pakistan and other jurisdictions where our service providers operate. Users requiring a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) may contact us at support@scoutix.io.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
