            <section class="policy-section" id="data-retention">
                <div class="section-number">Section 11</div>
                <h2>Data Retention &amp; Backups</h2>
                <p>We retain your personal data for as long as your account remains active and for a reasonable period thereafter to fulfil the purposes outlined in this policy.</p>

                <h3>Active Account Data</h3>
                <p>Account data, usage logs, and associated records are retained for the duration of your active subscription and for <strong>30 days</strong> following account cancellation, to allow for reactivation or dispute resolution. After this period, your personal data is permanently deleted from active production systems.</p>

                <h3>Billing &amp; Financial Records</h3>
                <p>Transaction records, invoice history, and billing data may be retained for up to <strong>7 years</strong> from the date of transaction to comply with financial recordkeeping obligations and tax regulations applicable in Pakistan and other relevant jurisdictions.</p>

                <h3>Backup &amp; Archival Systems</h3>
                <p>Our cloud infrastructure providers maintain automated backup systems for disaster recovery purposes. Personal data deleted from active systems may persist in encrypted backup archives for an additional period of up to <strong>90 days</strong> before being overwritten or permanently purged during routine backup rotation cycles. We do not use backup archives to restore or reactivate deleted accounts.</p>

                <h3>Anonymized Data</h3>
                <p>Aggregated, anonymized usage statistics and analytics data — which cannot reasonably be used to identify any individual — may be retained indefinitely for platform improvement purposes.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="cookies">
                <div class="section-number">Section 12</div>
                <h2>Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h2>
                <p>Scoutix uses cookies and similar technologies to operate the Service. We use three categories:</p>
                <p><strong>Essential Cookies:</strong> Required for authentication, session management, and core platform functionality. These cannot be disabled without impacting your ability to use the Service.</p>
                <p><strong>Functional Cookies:</strong> Remember your preferences such as language settings and UI configuration between sessions.</p>
                <p><strong>Analytics Cookies:</strong> Collect aggregated, anonymized data about how the platform is used to help us improve the Service. You may opt out of analytics cookies through your browser settings or account preferences without affecting core functionality.</p>
                <p>We do not use advertising cookies. We do not allow third-party advertisers to place cookies through our platform.</p>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <section class="policy-section" id="do-not-track">
                <div class="section-number">Section 13</div>
                <h2>Do Not Track Signals</h2>
                <p>Some browsers include a "Do Not Track" (DNT) feature that signals to websites that you prefer your browsing activity not be tracked. Scoutix does not currently respond to browser Do Not Track signals, as there is no consistent or legally binding industry standard for how such signals should be interpreted or honoured.</p>
                <p>We do not engage in cross-site behavioral tracking or share user data with advertising networks. If you wish to limit tracking, you may configure cookie preferences through your browser settings or opt out of analytics cookies through your Scoutix account settings.</p>
            </section>

